<title>JAPAN: Japan buys 60,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 T barley.</title>
<headline>Japan buys 60,000 tonnes wheat, 20,000 T barley.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Food Agency said on Thursday it bought 60,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat and 20,000 tonnes of Australian barley in its weekly tender, all for January shipment. Details in tonnes:</p>
<p>WHEAT</p>
<p>Country    Quantity</p>
<p>U.S.	 60,000	   Dark northern spring   20,000</p>
<p> Hard red winter	  31,000</p>
<p> Western white	     9,000</p>
<p>BARLEY</p>
<p>Australia  20,000	   Feed			 20,000</p>
</text>
